
# Code Structure

```
./
├── Makefile # Script to run the whole lab
├── retrieve.py # Script to retrieve the data from the stats.txt
├── Arch_Lab02.pdf # Lab report
├── [res] # Directory to store the results
|   ├── cmov-localbp # Directory to store the results of cmov with localBP
|   ├── cmov-tournamentbp # Directory to store the results of cmov with tournamentBP
|   ├── ncmov-localbp # Directory to store the results of ncmov with localBP
|   ├── ncmov-tournamentbp # Directory to store the results of ncmov with tournamentBP
├── pred # Directory to store the custom predictor
|   ├── replay.cc # The source code of the custom predictor
|   ├── replay.hh # The header file of the custom predictor
|   ├── SConscript # The SConscript file of the custom predictor
|   ├── BranchPredictor.py # The BranchPredictor.py file of the custom predictor
├── bin # Directory to store the binaries from different platform
|   ├── core
|   |   ├── cmov-slow-i5 # The binary compiled on Core i5
|   |   ├── ncmov-slow-i5 # The binary compiled on Core i5
|   ├── xeon
|   |   ├── cmov-slow-5118 # The binary compiled on Xeon 5118
|   |   ├── ncmov-slow-5118 # The binary compiled on Xeon 5118
├── README # here
├── cmov # The binary of the program to be tested
├── ncmov # The binary of the program to be tested
├── cmov.c # The source code of test (gem5, 10000 iters)
├── cmov.s # The assembly code of test
├── cmov-slow # The binary of the program to be tested
├── ncmov-slow # The binary of the program to be tested
├── cmov-slow.c # The source code of test  (gem5, 1000000000 iters)
├── cmov-slow.s # The assembly code of test
├── sample_res # Sample results reserved for checking
|   ├── ... Structure same as `./res` (trace.out and pipeview.out are not reserved, for they are too big)
```
`[xxx]` means it only exists when you at least run the codes for one time.


# Prepare the env

- gem5 22.1.0.0 build with X86-ISA
- GNU make 4.2.1


Then please the set the environment variable:
``` 
export GEM5_ROOT=<path_to_gem5_root>
e.g.
export GEM5_ROOT=/home/comparch48/gem5
```

# Run the codes
Make sure the gem5 build ready and the environment variable is set.

Then press the launch button!
```
make makeslow
make makegem5
make run-native
make run-gem5
make retrieve
```

You can get your results in the `./res` directory.
**A copy is reserved for checking in `./sample_res`.**

If you want to use the custom predictor, please run:
(If the Makefile is not compatable on your machine, please run the commands manually.)
```
make register-new-pred
make run-new-pred
```

If you want to check the assembly code, please run:
```
make dumpslow
make dumpgem5
```

If you want to inspect the trace, please run:
```
less -r ./res/xxxxxxx/pipeview.out
e.g.
less -r ./res/ncmov-localbp/pipeview.out
```

If you want to clean the results, please run:
```
make clean-result
```



